 "interpretation": "Vaeshákh (the first month of the Bengali calendar) symbolizes the arrival of Divine renewal, sweeping away stagnation and spiritual slumber (jad́imá). For centuries, humanity wandered in ignorance and suffered under the blows of relentless time (kála), weeping even in the illusory sleep of máyá. But with the advent of spiritual light (the image of the Vaeshákha full moon - Buddha Púrńimá), the fear of doom dissolves, the dawn of a new era shows humanity the path, and all creation (the horizon) is transfigured in joy.",
